Rationale for this change
timestamp-micros is handled by an explicit branch in _convert_logical_type`:

      iceberg-python/pyiceberg/utils/schema_conversion.py

        Lines 379 to 383
      in
      d37149c

           elif logical_type == "timestamp-micros":

               if avro_logical_type.get("adjust-to-utc", False) is True:

                   return TimestamptzType()

               else:

                   return TimestampType()

That also honors adjust-to-utc, so the mapping entry was never used.
Are these changes tested?
Are there any user-facing changes?
